## Known v0.1 limitations (encoded into this repo)

- `RecordingPreset.factoryDefault.audioSources = .sysOnly` — only
  records system audio by default. Default `.both` would activate
  the partially-broken AVAudioEngine mixer in
  `Sources/Core/Encoding/AudioMixer.swift` (look for the "KNOWN
  ISSUE" comment + `useEnginePath = false` flag).
- v0.2 mixer rewrite is the highest-priority follow-up. Two
  candidate approaches in the file's comment header.

## What to do BEFORE making changes

1. **Read at least the spec section relevant to your change.** If
   you're touching capture code, read research.md R1/R2 + the
   relevant US story. If you're touching UI, read
   contracts/ui-surfaces.md.
2. **Check if there's a relevant task** in tasks.md. If yes, mark
   it `[X]` after completing.
3. **Check the constitution** for any non-negotiable principle that
   touches your change. NON-NEGOTIABLE principles (I and III) cannot
   be relaxed without a constitution amendment.
4. **Use commit messages that link back to spec/plan refs**
   (e.g., `fix(audio): align AudioMixer with FR-011 (research.md R2)`).

## What changes belong in spec vs. here

| Change type | Goes in `home-spec` | Goes here |
|---|---|---|
| New user story / new feature | spec.md update + tasks.md | implementation Swift |
| Behavior change to existing FR | spec.md FR text update | implementation Swift |
| Implementation detail change (refactor) | (nothing) | Swift |
| Build / signing / dev tooling | troubleshooting.md note | scripts + project.yml |
| New "known issue" you discovered | troubleshooting.md | code workaround |
| New decision / tradeoff | research.md (new R{N}) | implementation |

If unsure, write the change in this repo first then ask whether it
needs a spec mirror. Don't silently drift the implementation away
from the spec.
